# CODEOWNERS (Task 042)
#
# WHAT THIS FILE IS FOR
# ---------------------
# Two gates resolve an owner from it and neither can do anything useful without
# it:
#   * `tools/npm-audit-gate.mjs` assigns a dependency advisory to a team, and
#     reports "No owner is assigned" - loudly, in the job summary - while any
#     handle below is still CHANGE_ME.
#   * `gitleaks` findings on a PR touching `deploy/` or the workflows are
#     reviewed by whoever owns those paths.
#
# >>> REPLACE EVERY `CHANGE_ME` HANDLE BEFORE ENABLING THE GATES ON A REAL REPO <<<
# The gate does not fail on a placeholder (a repository whose owner is not known
# yet is a normal state, and failing on it would mean the audit job is red before
# anyone has done anything). It says so in the report instead, because a finding
# assigned to `@CHANGE_ME/frontend` reads as assigned and is not.
#
# ORDER MATTERS: the LAST matching pattern wins, exactly as GitHub resolves it.
# `frontend/` appears before `frontend/package-lock.json` on purpose - the
# lockfile is a frontend concern, but its own team is the one that has to be able
# to run `npm audit fix` without asking anybody, so it gets the more specific
# rule. Reversing these two lines silently reassigns every lockfile finding to
# the frontend team.
#
# Keep this file in step with `docs/ci-branch-protection.md` ("Owners"), which
# records the same mapping in prose for the humans who set up branch protection.

# Default: the engineering team owns anything not claimed below.
*                                       @CHANGE_ME/engineering

